      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(exa): resolve web search SecretRefs at runtime",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users configuring Exa web search with an env-backed SecretRef could have that configured credential bypassed or treated inconsistently at runtime. If the configured SecretRef was missing, Exa could fall back to ambient `EXA_API_KEY` instead of failing closed.\n\nAI-assisted: yes.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe Exa runtime now uses the shared web-search credential resolver, which accepts literal credentials, resolves env SecretRefs, preserves the documented `EXA_API_KEY` fallback only when no credential is configured, and treats an explicit but unresolved SecretRef as authoritative. This keeps the fix inside the Exa provider runtime and avoids adding a new generic provider-auth path.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can configure Exa web search with an env SecretRef and expect runtime execution to use that resolved value. Misconfigured or unavailable SecretRefs now fail closed instead of silently using a different ambient Exa key.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/exa/src/exa-web-search-provider.test.ts` - 1 file passed, 21 tests passed.\n- `OPENCLAW_OXLINT_SKIP_PREPARE=1 node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs extensions/exa/src/exa-web-search-provider.runtime.ts extensions/exa/src/exa-web-search-provider.test.ts` - passed.\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check extensions/exa/src/exa-web-search-provider.runtime.ts extensions/exa/src/exa-web-search-provider.test.ts` - passed.\n- `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD` - passed.\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode branch --base upstream/main --engine claude` - clean after the added config-record SecretRef test.\n\n## Proof\n\n- Live open PR changed-files collision check completed before editing: scanned 2,762 open PRs and deep-checked 44 large PRs; no overlap with `extensions/exa/src/exa-web-search-provider.runtime.ts` or nearby Exa web-search tests/surfaces.\n- Topic search found related open secret-target registry work for installed plugin config targets, but no open PR touching the Exa runtime/test files and no same runtime `tools.web.search.exa.apiKey` SecretRef fallback fix.\n- Focused config matrix test now covers literal configured key precedence, documented `EXA_API_KEY` fallback when no key is configured, env SecretRef resolution through the Exa search config record, and fail-closed behavior for unavailable env/non-env SecretRefs.\n",
        "branch": "llagy007/exa-search-secretref-runtime-20260712",
